Similarly, for n-digit numbers, the total is sum_{d1=1}^9 (d1^{n-1}).

But wait, that's only if the first digit is d1, and the rest can be any digits less than d1. So for each d1, the number of possibilities is (d1)^(n-1). Because each of the remaining (n-1) digits can be any digit from 0 to d1-1. So for each d1, the count is (d1)^(n-1). 

So for a number with n digits, the total number of Snake numbers is sum_{d1=1}^9 (d1^{n-1}).


